<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Venetian Cyprus</h1><p class="st-meta">1489 CE – 1571 CE · capital Nicosia</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Cyprus under the Republic of Venice from 1489 to 1571, a heavily fortified frontier colony lost to the Ottomans in a famous siege of Famagusta.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Venetian influence in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-cyprus">Kingdom of Cyprus</a> grew through the marriage of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-ii-of-cyprus">James II</a> to the Venetian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catherine-cornaro">Catherine Cornaro</a>. After his death and that of their infant son, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> controlled Catherine's government, and in 1489 forced her to abdicate and cede the island to the Republic.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>A Venetian lieutenant and councillors ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicosia">Nicosia</a>, keeping the old Frankish nobility while taxing heavily. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a> exported <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a>, salt and wine, and paid tribute to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk-sultanate">Mamluk Egypt</a> and later the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>. Fearing invasion, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> rebuilt the walls of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/genoese-famagusta">Famagusta</a> and in 1567 built new star-shaped bastions around Nicosia.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> invaded in 1570. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicosia">Nicosia</a> fell in September 1570, and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/genoese-famagusta">Famagusta</a> surrendered in August 1571 after a long siege; its commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marco-antonio-bragadin">Marco Antonio Bragadin</a> was flayed alive. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a> became an Ottoman province.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/venetian-cyprus.jpg" alt="Venetian Cyprus" width="320" height="218"><figcaption>Image: Samhanin · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_Venetian_Cyprus.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1489 CE – 1571 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Nicosia</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Eastern Orthodox Christianity, Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Greek, Venetian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/cyprus">Cyprus</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Cyprus (Venetian)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1530&amp;focus=venetian-cyprus" aria-label="Venetian Cyprus on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5525 906 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Venetian Cyprus lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5845 1162L5845 1162M5845 1162L5293 831M5845 1162L5709 970"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5845 1162h0M5293 831h0M5709 970h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5845 1162h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5845 1162h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Nicosia. <a href="/atlas?year=1530&amp;focus=venetian-cyprus">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
